(RESERVE BANK OF INDIA) Tj
T*
(DEPARTMENT OF REGULATION, CENTRAL OFFICE, MUMBAI) Tj
T*
(RBI/2024-25/155 DoR.ORG.REC.65/21.04.158/2024-25) Tj
T*
(September 29, 2024) Tj
T*
(Master Direction on Outsourcing of Information Technology Services) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Prohibited Outsourcing Activities: Regulated Entities shall not outsource core management functions, including the decision-making) Tj
T*
(authority on credit sanction, overall risk management, compliance oversight, and internal audit functions. The ultimate responsibility) Tj
T*
(for outsourced IT operations rests entirely with the Board and Senior Management of the RE.) Tj
T*
(2. Due Diligence and Concentration Risk: REs shall perform rigorous financial, operational, and cybersecurity due diligence on service) Tj
T*
(providers prior to signing outsourcing agreements. Material outsourcing arrangements must evaluate concentration risk and avoid sole-vendor) Tj
T*
(dependency across core banking modules.) Tj
T*
(3. Data Sovereignty and Cross-Border Storage: The primary transactional databases and financial customer records of REs must reside) Tj
T*
(within the territorial borders of India. Where cross-border support or analytics is permitted, the service provider contract must) Tj
T*
(explicitly guarantee that the Reserve Bank and its appointed auditors have unrestricted right of inspection and audit of systems.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
9 0 obj
<< /Length 919 >>
stream
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 720 Td
13 TL
(4. Business Continuity and Disaster Recovery: Material IT outsourcing arrangements must include defined Recovery Time Objectives) Tj
T*
(\(RTO\) and Recovery Point Objectives \(RPO\). For critical payment and customer-facing banking services, the RTO shall not exceed two hours) Tj
T*
(and RPO shall not exceed 15 minutes. Disaster recovery drills with service providers must be conducted at least once annually.) Tj
T*
(5. Termination and Exit Clauses: All outsourcing contracts must incorporate clear exit strategies, transitional assistance requirements,) Tj
T*
(and guaranteed return or destruction of proprietary data within 30 days of contract termination.) Tj
T*
(6. Sub-contracting Authorization: The service provider shall not sub-contract any material component of the outsourced service to a) Tj
T*
(third party without prior written consent from the Regulated Entity.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
10 0 obj
<< /Length 877 >>
stream
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 720 Td
13 TL
(7. Cloud Computing Architecture and Encryption: Regulated Entities migrating workloads to public or multi-tenant cloud service) Tj
T*
(providers must ensure that data at rest and data in transit is encrypted using advanced algorithms \(AES-256 minimum\). Customer-managed) Tj
T*
(encryption keys \(CMEK\) must be held by the RE.) Tj
T*
(8. Audit and Access Rights: Contracts with IT service providers must explicitly grant the Regulated Entity, its internal and external) Tj
T*
(auditors, and the Reserve Bank's supervisory teams unhindered physical and logical access to relevant infrastructure, logs, and staff.) Tj
T*
(9. Incident Notification by Vendors: IT service providers must contractually commit to notify the Regulated Entity of any security incident,) Tj
T*
(data breach, or unauthorized access within two hours of detection.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
11 0 obj
<< /Length 858 >>
stream
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 720 Td
13 TL
(10. Service Level Agreements \(SLAs\): Comprehensive metrics for system availability, response time, bug fixes, and patch management) Tj
T*
(must be incorporated into SLAs with predefined financial penalties for non-compliance.) Tj
T*
(11. Offshore Service Providers: Where the service provider is located outside India, the RE must evaluate the legal and geopolitical risks) Tj
T*
(of the foreign jurisdiction and ensure that regulatory actions by foreign authorities cannot block Indian bank records.) Tj
T*
(12. Board Review of Outsourcing: A comprehensive inventory of all material IT outsourcing arrangements and vendor performance reports) Tj
T*
(shall be presented to the Board of Directors at least once every financial year.) Tj
T*
(Yours faithfully,) Tj
T*
(\(Charulatha S. R.\)) Tj
T*
(Chief General Manager) Tj
T*
ET
